        "title": "The Rainy-Day Delivery",
        "body": "Nora promised to deliver books to the neighborhood reading club. On Saturday, dark clouds gathered. She put the books in a cardboard box and stepped outside. Before she reached the gate, rain began soaking the box. Nora hurried back inside. She dried the covers and moved the books into a waterproof bag. Her brother offered a ride in his bicycle trailer, but the trailer had no cover. Nora thanked him and waited until the rain stopped. At the club, a volunteer smiled at the dry books. Nora was late, but every book could still be read. The next week, she checked the forecast before packing."
